WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.751
Someone has reversed into Alex's car.

2
00:00:02.751 --> 00:00:08.657
A claim involves a driver, an insurer and a repairer, and usually a lot of forwarded email.

3
00:00:09.507 --> 00:00:15.306
Alex starts the claim in their own pod: what happened, photos, and the other driver's details.

4
00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:23.800
Alex reports it to the insurer and grants access to three things: the driving licence, the policy, and this claim.

5
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.769
The claims handler checks the licence and the cover.

6
00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:31.129
Both are signed credentials, so there is nobody to ring.

7
00:00:31.129 --> 00:00:33.949
Then they write a damage report into the claim.

8
00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.394
The car needs a body shop.

9
00:00:38.303 --> 00:00:43.763
Alex gives the repairer the damage report and the photos, and nothing more, until the job is done.

10
00:00:44.613 --> 00:00:49.393
The workshop opens the job, reads those two things, and writes its estimate back.

11
00:00:50.377 --> 00:00:55.246
The repairer did not see the licence, the policy, or the other driver's details.

12
00:00:55.246 --> 00:00:56.463
It had no reason to.

13
00:00:57.314 --> 00:01:01.363
The insurer reads the estimate where the repairer wrote it, and approves it.

14
00:01:03.478 --> 00:01:06.351
The repair is finished and the invoice is filed.

15
00:01:06.351 --> 00:01:09.643
The repairer's grant was for this job, so it ends here.

16
00:01:10.492 --> 00:01:13.941
If the workshop opens the photos again, the pod refuses.

17
00:01:14.791 --> 00:01:18.575
Alex closes the claim and withdraws the insurer's access to it.

18
00:01:18.575 --> 00:01:20.677
The insurer still reads the policy.

19
00:01:20.677 --> 00:01:22.419
It no longer reads the claim.

20
00:01:23.269 --> 00:01:26.900
Three parties, two grants, each scoped to one job.

21
00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:31.513
We are looking for insurers to help shape this model.

22
00:01:31.513 --> 00:01:34.493
Join the EDMA Solid Community of Practice.
